{"id":"jehucal","name":"Jehucal","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:jehucal"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Jehucal","text":"Able, the son of Shelemiah. He is also called Jucal (Jer. 38:1). He was one of the two persons whom Zedekiah sent to request the prophet Jeremiah to pray for the kingdom (Jer. 37:3) during the time of its final siege by Nebuchadnezzar. He was accompanied by Zephaniah (q.v.)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H8018","lemma":"שֶׁלֶמְיָה","xlit":"Shelemyâh","gloss":"Shelemjah, the name of nine Israelites","kjv":"Shelemiah","count":2,"share":0.67},{"strong":"H3414","lemma":"יִרְמְיָה","xlit":"Yirmᵉyâh","gloss":"Jirmejah, the name of eight or nine Israelites","kjv":"Jeremiah","count":2,"share":0.67}],"verses":["Jer.37.3","Jer.38.1","Jer.38.4"],"related":[{"id":"hananiah","type":"lexical","strong":"H8018","why":"both lead with שֶׁלֶמְיָה (H8018)"},{"id":"shelemiah","type":"lexical","strong":"H8018","why":"both lead with שֶׁלֶמְיָה (H8018)"},{"id":"azriel","type":"lexical","strong":"H3414","why":"both lead with יִרְמְיָה (H3414)"},{"id":"ebed-melech","type":"lexical","strong":"H3414","why":"both lead with יִרְמְיָה (H3414)"},{"id":"jeremiah","type":"lexical","strong":"H3414","why":"both lead with יִרְמְיָה (H3414)"},{"id":"pathros","type":"lexical","strong":"H3414","why":"both lead with יִרְמְיָה (H3414)"}],"works":[]}
